.po 1i
.TH EXIT 1C UCB
.V 08/15/84 16:50:23
.\"@[$]exit.1C	1.6	08/15/84 16:50:23 - Zilog Inc.
.ad
.SH NAME
exit \- exit a shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B exit
.br
.B exit
.I (expression)
.SH DESCRIPTION
The shell exits either with the value of the
.I status
variable (first form) or with the value of the specified
.I  expression
(second form). This command is ignored if the 
.I ignoreexit
variable is set.
.SH SEE ALSO
break(1C),
logout(1C).
.br
\fIThe C Shell\fR in the ZEUS Utilities Manual.
